      "title": "Caesar Cipher Relay Network",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() \n{\n    int n, q;\n    cin >> n >> q;\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    vector<long long> diff(n + 1, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < q; i++) \n    {\n        int l, r;\n        long long k;\n        cin >> l >> r >> k;\n        k %= 26;\n        diff[l] += k;\n        if (r + 1 < n) diff[r + 1] -= k;\n    }\n    vector<long long> shift(n);\n    shift[0] = diff[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) \n    {\n        shift[i] = shift[i - 1] + diff[i];\n    }\n    string ans = s;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) \n    {\n        long long finalShift = (shift[i] + shift[n - 1 - i]) % 26;\n        int encrypted = s[i] - 'a';\n        int original = (encrypted - finalShift + 26) % 26;\n        ans[i] = char(original + 'a');\n    }\n    cout << ans << endl;\n    return 0;\n}",
      "statement": "A secret agency sends messages through multiple relay towers. Each tower applies a Caesar shift to only a specific part of the message. You are given an encrypted lowercase string s of length n.\nThere are q relay records. Each record contains: l r k\n\nThis means that during encryption, every character from index l to r was shifted forward by k. But there is a twist: After all relay shifts, the agency also performs a mirror Caesar lock:\nFor every index i: final_shift[i] = total_shift[i] + total_shift[n - 1 - i]\n\nThen the character at index i is shifted forward by final_shift[i].\n\nYou are given the final encrypted string. Your task is to recover the original string. Indexing is 0-based.\n\nSample Input:\n6 3\nkhoorx\n0 2 3\n2 5 1\n1 4 2\n\nSample Output:\ngzffjt\n\nExplanation:\nRelay shifts are applied on ranges.\n\nAfter calculating all range shifts, each position also receives the shift of its mirror index.\n\nSo index i uses:\n\nshift[i] + shift[n - 1 - i]\n\nTo decrypt, subtract this final shift from the encrypted character.",
