    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">A secret agency sends messages through multiple relay towers. Each tower applies a Caesar shift to only a specific part of the message. You are given an encrypted lowercase string s of length n.<br>There are q relay records. Each record contains: l r k<br><br>This means that during encryption, every character from index l to r was shifted forward by k. But there is a twist: After all relay shifts, the agency also performs a mirror Caesar lock:<br>For every index i: final_shift[i] = total_shift[i] + total_shift[n - 1 - i]<br><br>Then the character at index i is shifted forward by final_shift[i].<br><br>You are given the final encrypted string. Your task is to recover the original string. Indexing is 0-based.<br><br>Sample Input:<br>6 3<br>khoorx<br>0 2 3<br>2 5 1<br>1 4 2<br><br>Sample Output:<br>gzffjt<br><br>Explanation:<br>Relay shifts are applied on ranges.<br><br>After calculating all range shifts, each position also receives the shift of its mirror index.<br><br>So index i uses:<br><br>shift[i] + shift[n - 1 - i]<br><br>To decrypt, subtract this final shift from the encrypted character.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\">n q<br>s<br>l1 r1 k1<br>l2 r2 k2<br>...<br>lq rq kq</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\">original_string</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &lt;= n &lt;= 2 * 10^5<br>1 &lt;= q &lt;= 2 * 10^5<br>0 &lt;= l &lt;= r &lt; n<br>0 &lt;= k &lt;= 10^9<br>s contains only lowercase English letters</div>